CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*error.*$
--
C++20 requires-expression parameter binding when the requires-expression is a
conjunct of a larger constraint-expression ([expr.prim.req.general]/2).  A
concept of the shape `<concept-id> && requires(params){...}` -- the shape of
std::assignable_from, std::movable and std::copyable -- must bind the
requires-expression's parameters even though its #requires_params node is not at
the top of the constraint-expression.  Guards the recursive
requirement-parameter materialisation in instantiate_template.  See
doc/architectural/cpp-requires-expression-support.md.
